# dconf profile for every user on this device.
#
# It exists so the file next to it, /etc/dconf/db/local.d/01-taimen-sensors,
# is consulted at all: without a system-db line in the profile, dconf reads
# the user database and nothing else. "user-db:user" first keeps the user's
# own choices winning over these defaults, which is the point of setting a
# default rather than forcing a value.
#
# Why this is not a gschema override, which is the obvious mechanism and the
# one this device used to use: glib-compile-schemas will not let a second
# override file change a key an earlier one already overrode, and BOTH phosh
# (00_mobi.Phosh.gschema.override) and postmarketOS
# (00_postmarketos-base-ui-gnome.gschema.override) override
# ambient-enabled=false. Measured on the device: a taimen override sorting
# after them (99-) and a taimen override sorting before them (00-) BOTH lost,
# while a control key in the very same file that no 00_ file mentions took
# effect immediately. So filename ordering is not the lever it was documented
# to be, and auto-brightness was off no matter what that file said.
user-db:user
system-db:local
